h1 -- kbd privacy policy

p -- Effective October 14, 2026

p --
  Nothing you type leaves your device. kbd has no accounts, no analytics and no
  tracking, and the keyboard has no network access and does not use Full Access.

p --
  To work, kbd stores a few small files on your iPhone, inside the keyboard's
  own storage: words you add, email addresses you choose to remember, your emoji
  history, and numbers describing where your thumb lands on the keys. They never
  leave your phone, and deleting the app deletes them. kbd also reads your Text
  Replacements and contact names from iOS to offer as suggestions, and keeps
  them only in memory.

h2 -- Train swipes

p --
  If you opt in, the app sends your swipes on its sample sentences, the finger
  and setting you pick, and your phone's model, under a random ID. They may be
  published as an open dataset after 30 days. Delete them with that ID at
  lavalva.dev/app/kbd/training.

p -- Questions: kbd@lavalva.dev
